# The M2 smoke: sound, verified without ears. A click train is the source that makes timing
# visible — its onsets are exact samples, so a loop point that drifts moves an edge you can
# read. No fixture file is needed for any of it; the source is generated from this line.
{"t":"deck.load","deck":"a","source":{"gen":"click-train","secs":2,"hz":8}}
# An instance holds its own values, so each plugin is appended under a caller-minted id and then
# configured through that id — the same (instance, param) handoff a session restore uses (0030).
{"t":"effect.add","deck":"a","id":"flt","effect":"filter"}
{"t":"param.set","deck":"a","instance":"flt","param":"filter.cutoff","value":8000}
# A quarter-second loop over the first two clicks: four cycles per second of wall time.
{"t":"deck.loop","deck":"a","in":0,"out":0.25}
{"t":"param.set","deck":"a","param":"deck.gain","value":0.8}
{"t":"deck.play","deck":"a"}
# A second of audio time, so playback actually starts (a lookahead after the command) and
# comes round several times. The clock this waits on is ctx.currentTime — if the context
# were suspended in the headless host, this would hang rather than pass quietly.
{"wait":1}
# Append delay after the audio thread has reported several loop cycles: rack rewiring during
# playback gets a real-browser exercise without making the fixture wait any longer.
{"t":"effect.add","deck":"a","id":"dly","effect":"delay"}
{"t":"param.set","deck":"a","instance":"dly","param":"delay.time","value":0.05}
{"t":"param.set","deck":"a","instance":"dly","param":"delay.feedback","value":0.2}
{"t":"param.set","deck":"a","instance":"dly","param":"delay.mix","value":0.1}
{"probe":true}
{"peek":"a"}
{"t":"deck.stop","deck":"a"}
# Deck b is created here rather than assumed: a session boots with deck a alone (0029).
# Deck b proves a one-shot ends on its own: no loop, a short source, and deck.stopped
# arrives with reason "ended" without anything asking it to. The peek lands mid-sine — a
# constantly loud source, so the meter must read hot — which is what proves the read channel
# is wired through a real graph, not just returning its no-engine zeros (0014).
{"t":"deck.add","deck":"b","emoji":"🌴","name":"North Willow"}
{"t":"deck.load","deck":"b","source":{"gen":"sine","secs":0.5,"hz":220}}
{"t":"deck.play","deck":"b"}
{"wait":0.1}
{"peek":"b"}
{"wait":0.5}
# A loop below one render quantum is well-formed off the wire and impossible on the audio
# thread — a second of it owes a billion cycles. It is refused into no loop, and the log says
# so. If this ever wedges the page, the smoke times out, which is the point of sending it.
{"t":"deck.loop","deck":"b","in":0,"out":0.000000001}
{"wait":0.3}
